course: dictionary
lesson: 5838
title: Makeover
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A makeover is a big change that makes something look new and better. It can be a new hairstyle and clothes for a person, or new paint and furniture for a bedroom. «Makeover shows and influencers' "perfect" routines are often selling products; nobody needs a makeover to be worth something.» The clue is "worth something": a makeover changes how something looks, not how much it is worth.
explain: Read the words around the word. «Big "surprise" moments, like a makeover reveal, are sometimes filmed more than once; it can still be a happy day for the family.» A makeover reveal is the moment the new look is shown to everyone, and the family can still be happy even when filming happens more than once.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it in. "Nobody needs a new look to be worth something" still makes sense, so your meaning fits.
fact: A makeover is a big change to how a person, room, building or place looks.
fact: «Give something a makeover» means to change it so that it looks new and better.
fact: In an informal way, a makeover can be any big change that makes something better, as in «The team needs a makeover».
fact: «A complete makeover» means a change from top to bottom.
fact: Makeover TV shows and "perfect" online routines are sometimes trying to sell you something, so think about why they show a change.
exercise: «The old bedroom got a complete makeover, with new paint, a new bed and new curtains.» What is a makeover? | A map of the house | *A big change that makes something look new and better | A small mess left after painting | A sleepy night in the old bed
exercise: Mia says, «My gran's garden had a makeover.» What does it mean? | The garden was lost in the fog | *The garden was changed to look better | The garden was given a new name | The garden was dug up and left empty
exercise: Which of these is a makeover? | A trip to the shops | Reading a book in bed | *A new hairstyle and new clothes for a person | Counting to ten
test: «The team needs a makeover» means the team needs a big change to make it better. What does makeover mean in this sentence? | A sleepy team | Losing a game | *A big change to make it better | A bigger team
test: «It can still be a happy day for the family.» This shows that a makeover reveal can be... | A kind of food | Always sad | *A moment that can make people happy | Something nobody sees
exam: Jayden says a makeover means he must buy new clothes every week. Is he right? | Yes, but only for people, never rooms | No, because makeovers are always secret | *No, a makeover is one big change to how something looks | Yes, every makeover means new clothes
